.TH SYS_PROC_MAPS 2 "March 2026" "Substrate" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
sys_proc_maps \- list memory mappings for a process
.SH LIBRARY
System library (libsys, \-lsys)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/sysinfo.h>
.PP
.BI "int sys_proc_maps(pid_t " pid ", sys_map_t *" maps ", size_t *" count ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR sys_proc_maps ()
attempts to return virtual memory map entries for process
.IR pid .
Entries are written to
.I maps
and count is communicated through
.IR *count .
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, 0 is returned.
On error, a negative value is returned by the current implementation.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B ENOSYS
Current kernel implementation is a stub.
.SH NOTES
Wired in native dispatch, currently unimplemented in kernel.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sys_proc_info (2),
.BR mmap (2),
.BR pmap_stats (2)
